Extender FILEMGR buffered-reader init FUN_0000_5f17 (image 0x5f17): the buffer SIZE word
[0x5560] is the integer 0x400, but Ghidra base-lost the immediate into the host pointer
`s_KKKK_0000_0005 + 0x3fb` (= g_mem+fist_ext_base+0x400).  In the Route-1 host-pointers-in-slots
model that poisons [0x5560] into a huge host-pointer value; the `>>1` then yields garbage, and
every downstream `[0x5560] + [0x5564]` / `[0x5560] - x` in the buffered reader FUN_0000_5fbe /
terrain reader FUN_0000_643c computes an off-buffer address -> the observed 643c OOB write
(0xc3ee4a8; the bogus size == the 68475568-byte read count).  asm ground truth (objdump):
    5f17: mov  DWORD [0x5560], 0x400   ; SIZE = 0x400 (a bare immediate, NOT a pointer)
    5f21: shr  DWORD [0x5560], 1       ; SIZE >>= 1  -> 0x200
    5f2d: mov  ecx,[0x5560]
    5f33: cmp  ecx, 0x400 ; jbe 5f52   ; SIZE <= 0x400 -> use the static 0x5898 buffer
    5f52: mov  eax, 0x5898             ; static buffer ptr -> [0x5564]  (host ptr via &DAT_5898)
    5f5e: add  eax,[0x5560] ; [0x5568] = ptr + SIZE  (buffer END)
[0x5560] is thus an INTEGER size (0x200 after the shr); [0x5564]=host bufptr, [0x5568]=host end.
Keeping [0x5560] a small integer makes `[0x5564]+[0x5560]` a valid host end pointer and the
`(short)` reg-file truncations in 5fbe cancel correctly (bufptr and read cursor share high bits;
the remaining count < SIZE < 2^16).  Fix = store the literal 0x400 (and the `<= 0x400` bound as
< 0x401) instead of the base-lost host pointers; leaves [0x5560] a small integer masquerading as
a pointer, so no macro/type ripple.  Flat32-module base-loss-of-immediate class; never exercised
before op-0x18 (KDV streams via direct reads, not this buffered reader).
